# Benchmark diffs are data, not source.
#
# A unified diff means what its bytes say. Letting Git rewrite the line endings
# on checkout changes the measurement: converting change.diff to CRLF turns the
# small-change-sprawl scenario from 9 semantic lines into 2, because the
# firewall's presentation/semantic split reads line endings as presentation —
# correctly, since that is what §53 asks it to detect.
#
# So the benchmark would silently measure something different on a Windows
# clone than on CI, which is the one thing a benchmark must never do.
*.diff -text
*.patch -text
